From 2088a5dac87fec4490b86872c9add67e219185de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:25:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] agent: let an operator who is the jail hand unconfined
 jobs its GPUs

A rented GPU pod is a container with no engine and no /dev/kvm inside, so no
jail can be built there and no engine can pass a device; its operator runs
jobs with --sandbox none, and a job that asked for a GPU was refused. That
refusal protected the receipt, not the card: an unconfined job runs as the
agent's user and can already open whatever devices that user can.

--unconfined-gpus (CAIRN_AGENT_UNCONFINED_GPUS=1) on run, exec and install
lets a job that asks for none and for GPUs run there. Its receipt lists gpus
under unenforced beside isolation, with a note naming the flag, and the
registration's jobs block says unconfined_gpus. The flag is refused on a host
whose operator chose any jail, where it could do nothing; a jail still needs
an engine to pass a GPU. agent-demo.sh checks the refusal, the run, the
receipt and the environment file install writes.
